          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00003">
        <exercise id="888b0421-a3b8-4c69-954a-7b61207524da" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00008">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00026">Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para id="para-00027">Without graphing, find the coordinates of the vertex of \(y=(x−4)^2+8\) and determine if it opens up or down.</para>
            <para id="para-00028"> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00029">Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 4.</para>
            <para id="para-00030">The correct answer is is 4. The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="bbb6f97f-b144-4be0-89e9-52604b454621" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00009">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00031">Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para id="para-00032"> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00033"> Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 8.</para>
            <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is is 8. The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 8.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="798d9134-c715-4e30-8eda-95ddc060c136" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00010">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00035"> Does the graph open up or down? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00036">Correct! The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient (1).</para>
            <para id="para-00037">Incorrect. The correct answer is Up. The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient (1).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
