      <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
        <item>Are the patterns you noticed still happening? See if you can apply those patterns to the following equations.</item>
      </list>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00006">
        <exercise id="8fd2bb2b-35a9-49b3-93e0-6b1010b68b27" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00020">
          <problem id="prob-00020">
            <para id="para-00069">Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para id="para-00070"> For the equation \(y=\frac{1}{2}(x+3)^2−5\), what is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00019">
            <para id="para-00071">Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(–3\).</para>
            <para id="para-00072">The correct answer is is \(–3\). The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(–3\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="97021ac7-5208-432a-a6f5-432c6448485f" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00021">
          <problem id="prob-00021">
            <para id="para-00073">Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para id="para-00074"> For the equation \(y=\frac{1}{2}(x+3)^2−5\), what is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00020">
            <para id="para-00075">Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(-5\).</para>
            <para id="para-00076">The correct answer is is \(n\). The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(-5\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="1d9cfcdf-595c-471d-9307-16dd20ce2f36" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00022">
          <problem id="prob-00022">
            <para id="para-00077"> For the equation \(y=\frac{1}{2}(x+3)^2−5\), does the graph open up or down?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00021">
            <para id="para-00078">Correct! The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient \(\frac{1}{2})\). </para>
            <para id="para-00079">Incorrect. The correct answer is Up.The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient \(\frac{1}{2})\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="16199d79-2505-408f-b4ff-e5b931fa83bb" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00023">
          <problem id="prob-00023">
            <para id="para-00080">Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para id="para-00081"> For the equation \(y=-(x+100)^2+50\), what is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00022">
            <para id="para-00082">Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(–100\).</para>
            <para id="para-00083">The correct answer is is \(–100\). The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(–100\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a1771807-d7bb-465d-9019-eabb1fce4737" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00024">
          <problem id="prob-00024">
            <para id="para-00084">Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para id="para-00085"> For the equation \(y=-(x+100)^2+50\), what is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00023">
            <para id="para-00086">Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(50\).</para>
            <para id="para-00087">The correct answer is is \(n\). The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(50\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="7fc8f227-f6be-48a3-97bf-c9787f891f76" class="multiple-choice" id="exer-00025">
          <problem id="prob-00025">
            <para id="para-00088"> For the equation \(y=-(x+100)^2+50\), does the graph open up or down? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00024">
            <para id="para-00089">Correct! The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative coefficient \((-1)\).. </para>
            <para id="para-00090">Incorrect. The correct answer is Up. The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative coefficient \((-1)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
